{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sets-of-sequences","title":"Sets of sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"]},{"anchor":"Dictionaries-keyed-by-sequences","title":"Dictionaries keyed by sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"]},{"anchor":"Pattern-matching","title":"Pattern matching","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"]},{"anchor":"Extended-Modules","title":"Extended Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie"},{"type":"text","text":" is a set of sequences and a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" a dictionary keyed by them, both kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a trie (Fredkin, 1960): a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex paths spell the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keys. They answer the queries a hash set cannot: every key with a prefix"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(withPrefix:)"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" is O(1)), whether any key has one ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPrefix(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the longest key that is a prefix of a query ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"longestPrefix(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Tries","","let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys are any sequence of the symbol type and are stored as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Symbol]"},{"type":"text","text":". For text, the symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type decides what a step is: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Character>"},{"type":"text","text":" steps by grapheme cluster, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by scalar, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<UInt8>"},{"type":"text","text":" over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"utf8"},{"type":"text","text":" by byte, the fastest of the three, because comparing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes is cheaper than comparing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Character"},{"type":"text","text":"s. When the symbols are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its children sorted, so iteration is in lexicographic order; otherwise children come in the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were added."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","type":"reference"},{"text":" and a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","type":"reference"},{"text":" hold the same keys and answer the same queries,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the same names, in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): every chain of vertices with one child and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols, so there is a vertex per key and per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"branching point rather than per symbol. They suit keys with long shared prefixes, such as file","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths or URLs, and build faster and in less memory than a trie of the same keys.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A trie’s shape converts to Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree(_:)"},{"text":", and a radix tree’s to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"text":" of its vertices’ prefixes with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(_:)"},{"text":" (import Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trees"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module beside this one).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (Aho and Corasick, 1975) finds every occurrence of any of a set of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patterns in one pass over a text, in O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"z","type":"text"}]},{"text":") for ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":" symbols and ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"z"}]},{"text":" matches: a trie of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patterns with failure links. Its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is the automaton as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\").map(\\.patternIndex)   \/\/ [1, 0, 3]"]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"collection","externalID":"Tries","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","title":"Tries","modules":[{"name":"Tries"}]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries over sequences of any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tries"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/StatesView-swift.struct/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The symbol a goto edge reads, or nil for a failure edge."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"symbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ofEdgeAt","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.struct\/symbol(ofedgeat:)"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTree":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A set of sequences kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every chain of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"RadixTree","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtree"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/TrieDictionary":{"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/triedictionary","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"TrieDictionary","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"root-to-vertex paths spell the keys, each key’s vertex holding its value (Fredkin, 1960).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrieDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TrieDictionary","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trie","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"Trie","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A set of sequences kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paths spell the keys (Fredkin, 1960)."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTreeDictionary":{"abstract":[{"text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"chain of vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols, each key’s vertex holding its value.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","title":"RadixTreeDictionary","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RadixTreeDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"RadixTreeDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtreedictionary"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries over sequences of any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"Tries","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tries"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/statesView-swift.property":{"title":"statesView","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.property","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Symbol","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The automaton’s states as a directed graph: a vertex per state, numbered from 0 for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"root, a goto edge from each state to each of its trie children, and a failure edge from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each state but the root to its failure state. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" tells the two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"apart."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"statesView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV10StatesViewV","text":"StatesView","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trees":{"title":"Trees","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trees","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic"}}}